    {
      "name": "Week 4 - Password & Profile",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Forgot Password",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function() {\r",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);\r",
                  "});\r",
                  "pm.test(\"Response message is correct\", function() {\r",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include(\"reset link sent\");\r",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\r\n  \"email\": \"rahul@college.edu\"\r\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:8080/api/auth/forgot-password",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "8080",
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "forgot-password"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Triggers the forgot-password flow for a user account.\n\nThis endpoint accepts a registered email address and initiates password reset by generating a reset token or sending reset instructions.\n\nRequest body:\n\n- email: The registered user email address.\n    \n\nExample request:  \n{  \n\"email\": \"[rahul@college.edu](https://mailto:rahul@college.edu)\"  \n}\n\nExpected behavior:\n\n- Returns success if the reset flow is initiated.\n    \n- May return an error if the email is invalid or not registered.\n    \n\nNotes:\n\n- This endpoint should not expose whether an email is registered unless intentionally designed to do so.\n    \n- Commonly used before the Reset Password request."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Reset Password",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  ""
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\r\n  \"token\": \"bbb3c82e-3666-42f3-ba3a-71053d76fcac\",\r\n  \"newPassword\": \"NewPass@456\"\r\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:8080/api/auth/reset-password",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "8080",
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "reset-password"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Resets a user's password using a valid password reset token.\n\nThis endpoint is typically used after a user completes the forgot-password flow and receives a reset token.\n\nRequest body:\n\n- `token` (string): Password reset token issued by the system\n    \n- `newPassword` (string): The new password to set for the account\n    \n\nExpected behavior:\n\n- Returns success when the token is valid and the password is updated\n    \n- Returns an error if the token is invalid, expired, or already used"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Change Password",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  ""
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\r\n  \"oldPassword\": \"NewPass@456\",\r\n  \"newPassword\": \"SecurePass@123\"\r\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:8080/api/auth/change-password",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "8080",
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "change-password"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Changes the password for the currently authenticated user.\n\nThis endpoint requires the user to be logged in and authorized with a valid token. It verifies the user's current password before updating it to a new password.\n\nRequest body:\n\n- `oldPassword` — The user's current password\n    \n- `newPassword` — The new password to set for the account\n    \n\nExpected behavior:\n\n- Returns success when the current password is correct and the new password is accepted\n    \n- Returns an error if the current password is incorrect\n    \n- Returns an error if the new password does not meet password policy requirements\n    \n- Returns an error if the request is unauthenticated or the token is invalid"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Student Profile",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function() {\r",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);\r",
                  "});\r",
                  "pm.test(\"Profile has correct fields\", function() {\r",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();\r",
                  "    pm.expect(json.email).to.be.a(\"string\");\r",
                  "    pm.expect(json.name).to.be.a(\"string\");\r",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.not.have.property(\"passwordHash\");\r",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:8080/api/student/profile",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "8080",
              "path": [
                "api",
                "student",
                "profile"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Fetches the authenticated student's profile details.\n\nAuthorization:\n\n- Requires a valid Bearer token\n    \n\nEndpoint:\n\n- `GET /api/student/profile`\n    \n\nBase URL:\n\n- `http://localhost:8080`\n    \n\nDescription:  \nThis endpoint returns the profile information of the currently logged-in student. It is intended to be used after successful student login, when a token has been generated and stored in the environment variable.\n\nExpected behavior:\n\n- Returns the student's profile data when the token is valid\n    \n- Returns an unauthorized error if the token is missing or invalid\n    \n\nRequirements:\n\n- The `token` environment variable must contain a valid student access token\n    \n\nExample use case:\n\n1. Log in as a student\n    \n2. Store the returned token\n    \n3. Send this request to retrieve the student's profile information"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Student Profile",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function() {\r",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);\r",
                  "});\r",
                  "pm.test(\"Profile updated successfully\", function() {\r",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();\r",
                  "    pm.expect(json.phone).to.be.a(\"string\");\r",
                  "    pm.expect(json.email).to.be.a(\"string\");\r",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\r\n  \"phone\": \"9999999999\",\r\n  \"address\": \"123 New Street\",\r\n  \"city\": \"Hyderabad\",\r\n  \"pincode\": \"500001\"\r\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:8080/api/student/profile",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "8080",
              "path": [
                "api",
                "student",
                "profile"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Updates the authenticated student's profile details.\n\nThis endpoint allows a logged-in student to modify personal profile information such as phone number, address, city, and pincode. The request requires a valid bearer token in the Authorization header.\n\nAuthentication:\n\n- Bearer token required\n    \n\nRequest body fields:\n\n- `phone`: Updated phone number\n    \n- `address`: Updated street address\n    \n- `city`: Updated city name\n    \n- `pincode`: Updated postal code\n    \n\nExpected behavior:\n\n- Returns a success response when the profile is updated successfully\n    \n- Returns an error response if the token is missing/invalid or the input data is invalid"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
